model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "MCP session objects keep bearer and forwarded-grant revalidation on their own invocation database. Browser grants, discovery metadata and connection management use the existing API Worker's private service binding and its unchanged auth service. Replies preserve success and refusal schemas; transport and decode failures become AuthenticationUnavailable, with no fallback or cached authority. The production MCP upload guard rejects OAuth-provider, auth-adapter and migration engines. Unused schema and route factories are pure initializers; retained factories keep their original expressions. Generated MCP renderer assets and paths use pinned Bun. Skill frontmatter keeps the same YAML parser options and validation. Worker upload budgets stay unchanged. Purity wrappers surround declarations by name while retaining each current initializer body, including new billing and invocation fields; tree shaking cannot replace or simplify those public contracts. Private revoke replies retain the exact connection or agent ID returned by the shared service and preserve its typed refusals."
    }
  }
}
